'''II.''' ''n.'' '''1†.''' In ''music,'' same as ''treble.''

{{smaller block|Againe he heard that wondrous harmonie; . . .<br>The humane voices sung a ''triple'' hie,<br>To which respond the birds, the streames, the winde.
{{right|''Fairfax,'' tr. of Tasso's Godfrey of Boulogne, xviii. 24.}}
