'''2.''' ''pl.'' In ''change-ringing,'' changes rung on seven bells.

'''triple''' (trip′l), ''v.''; pret. and pp. ''tripled,'' ppr. ''tripling.'' [< F. ''tripler'' (= Pr. ''triplar''), make threefold, < ''triple,'' threefold, triple: see ''triple,'' ''a.''] '''I.''' ''trans.'' '''1.''' To make threefold or thrice as much or as many; treble.

{{smaller block|Enriched with annotations ''tripling'' their value.
{{right|''Lamb,'' Two Races of Men.}}}}

'''2.''' To be thrice as great or as many as.

{{smaller block|Their losse . . . did ''triple'' ours, as well in quality as in quantity.
{{right|''Hakluyt's Voyages.''}}}}

'''3.''' To alter from single or double to triple action, as a single or double expansion-engine into a triple expansion-engine; fit up with triple expansion-engines, as a vessel which has previously used a single or double expansion-engine.

'''II.''' ''intrans.'' To increase threefold.

